Last week Rhythm Culture visited the [Pinnacle Academic College](https://www.pinnacleacademiccollege.com.au/) for their annual Performing Arts Day activities. We had our [drumming and dancing school incursions](/school-incursions/) running simultaneously all day at the college. Students rotated and experienced different performing arts day activities such as arts and Auslan whilst also participating in one drum and dance session.

Familiar faces from last year's Performing Arts Day was such a treat and some of the students even remembered the call for the rhythm we did last time!

This year we explored the rhythm, Macru. All students learnt the call, a break and the drum patterns whilst also learning the dance to the same beats. We explored playing rhythms together and then playing different rhythms simultaneously. We also experienced the difference between playing with our ears and playing with our eyes. In the older classes we brought the drum and dance together. The students had an opportunity to test their memories and coordination by bringing it all together. There were lots of laughs!

All of the educators helped us deliver fun and engaging drumming and dancing workshops for the students at Pinnacle Academic College.

Thanks for having us Pinnacle Academic College we look forward to seeing you next time!!

Check us out at Pinnacle [here](https://www.facebook.com/permalink.php?story_fbid=975123633442350&id=276121103342610).
